  "settingsAwsAccountsSetupTitle": "How to set this up",
  "settingsAwsAccountsSetupStep1": "1. Sign in to the AWS console (console.aws.amazon.com), or create a free account if you don't have one.",
  "settingsAwsAccountsSetupStep2": "2. Open IAM → Users → Create user. Give it a name such as gratovo-gateway-deployer — it doesn't need console access, only programmatic access.",
  "settingsAwsAccountsSetupStep3": "3. Attach a permissions policy: the AWS managed policy \"AmazonAPIGatewayAdministrator\" is the simplest choice. For a tighter scope, a custom policy allowing just the apigateway:* actions is enough — this only ever creates/deletes HTTP APIs, integrations, routes and stages.",
  "settingsAwsAccountsSetupStep4": "4. Open the new user → Security credentials tab → Create access key → choose \"Application running outside AWS\". The secret access key is shown only once, so copy both values immediately.",
  "settingsAwsAccountsSetupStep5": "5. Paste the Access key ID and Secret access key below, add the region(s) you plan to deploy to (e.g. us-east-1, eu-west-1), and press Save.",
